{
	"name": "Leading Lure",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/control/debuff-energy-hold-blue-yellow.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 16th level, your fey has become quite adept at enthralling your foes, enough to lead them to their doom. Your fey can now move while using @UUID[Compendium.a5e-martial-artistry.class-features.Item.Zuj1k8dThPNrD9zA]{Enthrallment}, and creatures which have failed their saving throw against the effect must use their reaction to move up to their speed to remain within your enthrallment area if they would leave it outside their turn.</p><p>If your fey ends their movement in such a way that creatures who were not initially effected by the enthrallment begin their turn in its area, they must make a Wisdom save to avoid being swept up in the effect.</p>",
